# One patient per line (synthetic cases). Each column sees only its field:
# clinical, home or patient_says. The goal is the same for every column.
# H-1: fit, help at home in place, wants to go: every perspective agrees.
Patient: {"id": "H-1", "goal": "Assess readiness for discharge today", "clinical": "Admitted with a chest infection. Afebrile for 72 hours, oxygen saturation 96% on room air, oral antibiotics for 3 more days, CRP falling (140 to 22). Walking the ward independently.", "home": "Lives with her husband in a bungalow. Reablement team confirmed visits twice daily from the day of discharge for one week.", "patient_says": "I'm feeling much better and I'd like to go home to my husband."}
# H-2: medically fit, but lives alone upstairs and the care package starts next week.
Patient: {"id": "H-2", "goal": "Assess readiness for discharge today", "clinical": "Repaired hip fracture, day 6 after surgery. Wound clean, pain controlled on oral analgesia, observations stable. Mobilising 10 metres with a frame and one person assisting. Medically optimised.", "home": "Lives alone. Bedroom and only toilet are upstairs; physiotherapy notes she cannot yet manage stairs. Care package requested; the agency's earliest start is next Wednesday. No family nearby.", "patient_says": "I just want to go home. I'll manage somehow, I always have."}
# H-3: home is fine and the patient feels ready, but a new infection started this morning.
Patient: {"id": "H-3", "goal": "Assess readiness for discharge today", "clinical": "Planned discharge after a knee replacement. Overnight: new temperature 38.4, heart rate 112, CRP rising from 45 to 120. Blood cultures taken and intravenous antibiotics started this morning.", "home": "Lives with his wife and adult son in a ground-floor flat. Independent before admission; family can drive him and help with shopping.", "patient_says": "I feel a bit hot, but I'm fine, honestly. I want to get home today."}
# H-4: clinically fit, support in place, but the patient does not feel safe.
Patient: {"id": "H-4", "goal": "Assess readiness for discharge today", "clinical": "Admitted after a fall; no fracture, head CT normal. Observations stable for 48 hours, blood pressure medication adjusted, lying and standing blood pressure now normal. Physiotherapy: safe with a stick.", "home": "Lives alone in a ground-floor flat. Pendant alarm installed yesterday; carers booked morning and evening from today; daughter visits daily.", "patient_says": "I'm frightened to go back. Last time I lay on the floor all night before anyone came. I don't feel ready."}
# H-5: fit, independent, ready: every perspective agrees.
Patient: {"id": "H-5", "goal": "Assess readiness for discharge today", "clinical": "Day-2 after an uncomplicated laparoscopic appendicectomy. Eating and drinking, pain controlled on paracetamol, observations normal.", "home": "Lives with a partner; independent; no stairs problem; works from home.", "patient_says": "Can't wait to be in my own bed."}
